{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgwuz5dWL2aMpgowEETbH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Adjusting for both hospital and severity gives an ATE of about −5.09 days. The drug shortens hospital stays by roughly 5 days.\n\nHospital is a confounder because it determines both the chance of getting the drug (90% versus 10%) and how severe patients are. Severity is measured before treatment and strongly predicts days hospitalised, so including it is valid and makes the estimate more precise.\n\nI ran the regression `days ~ treatment + hospital + severity`:\n\n| Adjustment | Treatment coefficient |\n|---|---|\n| None | +14.15 (misleading, because of confounding) |\n| Hospital only | −10.80 |\n| Hospital and severity | −5.09 |\n\nThe hospital-only model is also a valid choice, since treatment is randomised within each hospital. I went with the fuller model because it uses severity, which explains much of the variation in days.\n\nANSWER: -5.09"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":545,"cache_read_input_tokens":30707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":545},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6563b5c3-1772-4071-bf64-5287f615f6ce","uuid":"253f5567-059f-4e0e-bde9-5d558382b194","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:16:52.164Z","request_id":"req_011Cgwuz5P7TrSd1pmdp4FSh"}
